# Pin shell scripts to LF regardless of the checkout platform's line-ending
# settings. A CRLF shell script fails cryptically on Linux/macOS ("invalid
# option" at whatever line has the first `\r`-corrupted flag), so this is
# not cosmetic. Verify with a byte count, never with grep -c:
#     python -c "import pathlib;b=pathlib.Path('tools/build.sh').read_bytes();print(b.count(13))"
# must print 0.
*.sh text eol=lf
